@startuml
title PayLink - Refund a Failed Payment

actor Customer
participant "PayLink System" as PayLink
participant "Biller Company" as Biller
actor Support

== Payment Failure ==

PayLink -> Biller: Send payment request

alt Biller rejects payment
    Biller --> PayLink: Payment failed
    PayLink -> PayLink: Update status to Failed
    PayLink -> PayLink: Release held money to wallet
    PayLink -> PayLink: Record refund in ledger and audit log
    PayLink --> Customer: Send SMS and Push notification

else Biller timeout
    Biller --> PayLink: No response
    PayLink -> PayLink: Set status to Unknown
    Note over PayLink
      Keep money held.
      Do not refund automatically.
    end note

    Biller -> PayLink: Send later callback

    alt Callback says Failed
        PayLink -> PayLink: Ignore duplicate callbacks
        PayLink -> PayLink: Update status to Failed
        PayLink -> PayLink: Release held money
        PayLink -> PayLink: Record in ledger and audit log
        PayLink --> Customer: Send failure notification

    else Callback says Success
        PayLink -> PayLink: Update status to Completed
        PayLink --> Customer: Send success notification
    end
end

== Refund Request for Completed Payment (FR-27) ==

opt Customer requests refund for completed payment
    Customer -> PayLink: Submit refund request
    PayLink -> Support: Send request for approval

    alt Support approves
        Support --> PayLink: Approve refund
        PayLink -> PayLink: Return money to customer wallet
        PayLink -> PayLink: Record money movement in ledger and audit log
        PayLink --> Customer: Refund confirmation

    else Support rejects
        Support --> PayLink: Reject refund
        PayLink --> Customer: Refund request rejected
    end
end

@enduml
